{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator decision 2026-09-07 (approved): the 29-key prefix re-spell of `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/...` rows in `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` is a sanctioned one-time maintenance edit for this package rename, carried in this change and named in the commit message. Rationale recorded: there is no CI lock on this file (enforcement is `--check` plus the unit tests, which pass when keys match paths), the honest alternative would be 29 `# mechanism-ok:` markers claiming a justified new mechanism for what is a rename, and the drain cannot express a rename. Reviewer check that the edit is value-preserving, to be run on both versions and diffed:\n\n```\npython -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(open(sys.argv[1])); print(\"\\n\".join(sorted(f\"{k.split(\"rebar_reconciler/\")[-1] if \"rebar_reconciler/\" in k else k.split(\"reconciler/\")[-1]} {v}\" for k,v in d[\"mechanisms\"].items() if k.startswith(\"autouse_fixture::tests/unit/re\"))))' .github/mechanism-baseline.json\n```\n\n(Adjust the top-level key name to the file's schema if it is not `mechanisms`; the intent is: strip the moved prefix, keep name and value, sort, diff main against the change, expect no difference.) Order inside the change: re-spell first, then `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` for the deleted autouse fixtures and the `tests/_engine_path.py` helper, then commit the baseline."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788809971538595138,"uuid":"2d67e1fd-2e62-481e-a936-77f509daca4a"}